                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Northern Indiana",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 17 at 7:44AM EDT until September 17 at 2:15PM EDT by NWS Northern Indiana",
                "description": "FFWIWX\n\nThe National Weather Service in Northern Indiana has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nAdams County in northeastern Indiana...\nHuntington County in northeastern Indiana...\nWells County in northeastern Indiana...\nSouthwestern Van Wert County in west central Ohio...\n\n* Until 215 PM EDT Thursday.\n\n* At 744 AM EDT, Scattered showers and thunderstorms continue across\nthe warned area. Doppler radar estimates between 2 and 5 inches of\nrain have fallen overnight. Another round of heavy rainfall is\npossible mid to late morning. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to\n2 inches are possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is already\noccurring.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Emergency management reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nHuntington, Bluffton, Decatur, Berne, Ossian, Geneva, Andrews,\nMarkle, Monroe, Lancaster, Preble, Nottingham, Zanesville,\nWillshire, Uniondale, Wren, Poneto, Vera Cruz, Murray and North\nOaks.\n\nSeveral reports of flooded roads and water rescues have been received\nthis morning.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
